demand for life-saving covid19 antibody  drugs is on the rise just four months  ago drug maker regeneron reported an  average of less than 5 000 dose  deliveries per week by september the  number increased to over hundred and  fifty thousand doses this is happening  as hospitalizations remain high in late  august over a hundred thousand covid19  patients were hospitalized nationwide a  daily average not seen since last  winter's surge  this comes as the delta variant sweeps  through the country and healthcare  systems become overwhelmed for those who  are vaccinated severe illness and  hospitalization due to the coronavirus  still remains rare but millions of  adults remain unvaccinated and for  high-risk patients who do get sick  doctors are increasingly turning to  antibody drugs to treat them to  understand why they've become so  critical in the fight against covid19  you need to understand how they work  when patients are infected by the new  coronavirus their immune systems should  produce antibodies these immune proteins  bind to the virus and prevent it from  spreading throughout the body antibodies  against covid19 do this by blocking what  is known as a spike protein on the  virus's surface this protein normally  helps the virus latch onto and infect  cells but for some people their immune  system doesn't produce enough antibodies  to fight off the virus or it doesn't  produce them fast enough this is where  antibody drugs like the ones that  regeneron and eli lilly produce come  into play to manufacture these drugs  researchers isolate what are called b  cells from a recovered patient's blood b  cells are a type of immune system cell  that makes antibodies in the lab the b  cells are then mixed with spike proteins  derived from the coronavirus once  scientists identify the b cells that are  best at latching on to the spike  proteins they isolate the genes inside  the cells that produce the most  effective antibodies these genes are  then placed inside cells and are grown  in bioreactors to create new antibodies  and these highly specific antibodies are  concentrated into a liquid solution and  then injected into sick covenant 19  patients this gives the body a temporary  boost of antibodies that help it fight  off infection  in clinical trials regeneron's drug  which is a combination of two types of  antibodies reduced the risk of  hospitalization or death by 70 percent  in people with mild to moderate symptoms  this is a big reason why treatment  guidelines from major health  organizations now recommend the use of  monoclonal antibody drugs for certain  patients so this is a major  breakthrough in the care of covid19  patients we have expanded our  our tools to treat patients with covid19  and this is our first recommendation for  a therapeutic for those patients with  mild moderate disease the world health  organization also recommends the use of  regeneron's antibody drug for patients  who are severely ill giving them this  additional antibody seems to show an  effect and what effect is that a  reduction in mortality as many hospitals  continue to be overwhelmed demand for  antibody drugs remains high  [Music]
 

